{
  "id": "moral-exclusion",
  "term": "moral exclusion",
  "definition": "Moral exclusion is the process of placing people outside one’s psychological boundary of justice, so normal moral rules and standards of fairness are not fully applied to them. People seen as useful for important goals are more likely to stay inside this boundary, while those seen as obstructive or expendable are more vulnerable to unfair or harmful treatment.",
